A||||3||NEO Cesek Racing||Rattling console||||1||
Z||000000||NEO Cesek Racing||11-01-2001||09:25 PM||||i know fieros vibrate a lot but my console behind the steering wheel vibrates up and down and rattles like hell. it's semi-annoying if i don' t have the radio up loud enough to drown it out. is there an easy fix for this or am i gonna wind up looking for a new dash at the bone yard?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-01-2001||10:03 PM||||I'm not sure exactly which part you are referring to but if you mean the main instrument cluster...... you might want to take the back cover off (three T-15 torx screws on the top, two down on the back, two 7mm hex head screws underneath (one on each side)) and check the mounting of the instrument cluster itself. There are two 10mm bolts that bolt into the dash frame which may have vibrated loose over time. There are also two 10mm bolts underneath (you need to remove the bottom shroud, under the steering column to find these) which also hold the cluster.<P>I'm guessing that will do the trick.....<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||NEO Cesek Racing||11-01-2001||10:07 PM||||yeah that's what i'm reffering to. i'll take a look at it tomorrow and let you know how it goes, thanks.||||reg||14
Z||000003||reddog||11-01-2001||10:57 PM||||Try taking it all apart and using soft rubber washers at all key mounting locations!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
